DESCRIPTION:Dive into the untold stories and complex strategies that led No
 rth Carolina to win big in the Revolution! In 1781\, North Carolina became
  critical to the fight for Independence. The patriot Continental Army was 
 led by brilliant Commissioned Officers such as Nathanael Greene\, Daniel M
 organ\, Light Horse Harry Lee\, William Washington\, and John Eager Howard
 \, who came from other states to fight in the Carolinas at the head of hig
 hly trained Continental infantry and cavalry and brave southern militia. T
 hey outfought and outmaneuvered the British Army for two critical months f
 rom mid-January to mid-March and achieved a vital link to the British surr
 ender at Yorktown six months later.\n\n \n\nFriday\, August 7\, 2026:\n\nB
 ethanie Historical Assoctiation\, 5530 Seidel St\, Bethania\, NC \n\nHisto
 rical Program and Keynote Address\n\n2p: Presentation of ColorsPanel Discu
 ssionKeynote Speaker: Zachary Deibel \n\nSaturday\, August 8\, 2026:\n\nSh
 allow Ford State Historic Siate (Lewisville\, NC)\n\nReenactment & Living 
 History\n\nKeynote Address & Luncheon\n\n8:15a: Reenactment Keynote Speake
 r: Dr. Wayne LeeLunch: Tavern at West Bend\, noon \n\nMore info: https://w
 ww.eventbrite.com/e/ncs-route-to-victory-in-the-revolution-tickets-1989917
 854871?aff=oddtdtcreator
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Race to the Dan: NC's Route to Victory in the Revolution
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/race-to-the-dan-ncs-route-to
 -victory-in-the-revolution
