DESCRIPTION:Ever been curious about mushrooms\, those weird and wild organi
 sms that unexpectedly pop out of the ground? This program is for you! This
  easy walk will introduce participants to the fungus family\, and everyone
  will have a chance to find living specimens and examine them closely.\n\n
 Attendees should dress for the weather and be prepared for a short hike on
  an uneven dirt tread. They are welcome to bring in samples of mushrooms f
 rom their own property for other participants to observe. Place any sample
 s in a paper bag\, and do not ingest any mushrooms found\, as they may be 
 poisonous.\n\nPlease note: collecting mushrooms is prohibited in North Car
 olina State Parks. There will be no foray as part of this program.
GEO:35.760718;-81.882276
LOCATION:Lake James State Park - Paddy's Creek Access\, Mountain Biking tra
 ilhead's parking lot in the Paddy's Creek Access
SUMMARY:Wild Mushroom Walk
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/wild-mushroom-walk
