DTSTART:20260810T160000Z
DTEND:20260810T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join Us!\n\nEnhance your teaching with a dynamic professional d
 evelopment session designed for Middle and High School Social Studies and 
 History educators seeking to teach about the history of North Carolina sch
 ool desegregation in the classroom. This session will be led by Dr. Shafan
 tae Desinord\, the Education and Interpretation Specialist for the North C
 arolina African American Heritage Commission. The session will offer in-de
 pth insights into the role of North Carolina leaders who stood on the fron
 t lines not only to push for institutions where African Americans could at
 tend and receive an education but also to play a major role in school dese
 gregation in North Carolina and nationally. Primary source materials from 
 leaders such as Dr. Charlotte Hawkins Brown\, Dorothy Counts\, Dr. John Ho
 pe Franklin\, Pauli Murray\, Julius Chambers\, and Floyd McKissick will be
  analyzed during the session.\n\nWhy Attend?\n\nEarn .5 hours of CEU credi
 t to help meet state licensure renewal requirements\, specifically by deve
 loping an understanding of African American history.Align your teaching wi
 th the North Carolina Standard Course of StudyGain expert strategies and r
 esources to bring compelling historical narratives into your classroom.Fos
 ter critical thinking and historical empathy among students as they explor
 e the struggles and triumphs of school desegregation.All session attendees
  will receive a complimentary copy ofSarah Keys Evans: The Power of Quiet 
 Courage by Amy NathanSession Details\n\nDay & Time: August 10th (12 pm- 1 
 pm) Place: VirtualDon't miss this opportunity to connect with fellow educa
 tors and deepen your understanding of the history of school desegregation.
  Register today!
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:North Carolina's Trailblazers Who Fought for School Desegregation A
 cross the State Through Educational\, Legal\, and Community Efforts
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/north-carolinas-trailblazers
 -who-fought-for-school-desegregation-across-the-state-through-educational-
 legal-and-community-efforts
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
