DESCRIPTION:Have fun wile learning about water literacy with this engaging 
 and informative Project WET Foundations workshop! Participants will receiv
 e a Foundations of Water Literacy guide with activities and resources to s
 upport water literacy in the classroom. Ideal for K-8 educators. This work
 shop qualifies for Criteria I or II in the NCEE certification Program.\n\n
 The Foundations of Water Education Guide from Project WET features 12 of i
 ts most popular\, hands-on activities designed to build water literacy in 
 students. Covering key topics like watersheds\, groundwater\, ecology\, an
 d water resource management\, these engaging lessons align with the Princi
 ples of Water Literacy to deepen understanding of our most vital resource.
  Each activity includes step-by-step instructions\, academic correlations\
 , and interactive learning experiences that foster critical thinking and p
 roblem-solving. This essential guide lays the groundwork for water educati
 on\, with more resources coming soon to expand on Project WET’s comprehe
 nsive curriculum.\n\nTo register: Email Monique.McKoy@ncparks.gov
GEO:35.477861;-76.901851
LOCATION:Goose Creek State Park
SUMMARY:Foundations of Water Education\, 12 lessons
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/foundations-of-water-educati
 on-12-lessons
