DESCRIPTION:Experience North Carolina farming culture and history at Duke H
 omestead! We’ll be harvesting our tobacco out of the field and demonstra
 ting the process of tobacco looping. Visitors are welcome to try their han
 d at these activities\, or to chat with an interpreter in the historic bui
 ldings.\n\nThis event is free to the public. It will be a free-flowing eve
 nt from 10am-2pm.\n\nThe Duke Homestead Education and History Corporation\
 , the volunteer non-profit support group for Duke Homestead\, will also be
  hosting a barbecue lunch fundraiser on August 22. Individual meal tickets
  can be purchased in advance or at the door\, and the meals are available 
 for both take-out or eating in the site’s picnic area. All proceeds of t
 he lunch will be used to supplement Duke Homestead’s special events\, si
 te maintenance\, and staff development. Tickets can be purchased in person
  at the site’s gift shop or at the event.\n\nThe $12 ticket includes pul
 led pork BBQ\, green beans\, potatoes\, utensils\, salt\, pepper\, and hot
  sauce. Bottled water and canned soft drinks will be available for $2 each
 .
