DESCRIPTION:The Elk Knob Community Heritage Organization (EKCHO) announces 
 that the 19th annual Headwaters Community Day Festival will return to Elk 
 Knob State Park on Saturday\, August 22nd\, 2026 from 11am to 3pm. \nThe H
 eadwaters Community Day Festival is a gathering to celebrate the area’s 
 unique culture and foodways. The activities start at 11 am and include liv
 e music\, local crafters\, farmers\, and other artisans demonstrating thei
 r work. At noon\, the High Country’s largest potluck dinner will be serv
 ed\, featuring dozens of local dishes. The public is encouraged to bring t
 heir own dish to share. \nElk Knob Community Heritage Organization (EKCHO)
  is a 501c(3) organization that is sponsoring the festival in partnership 
 with Elk Knob State Park. For more information contact Jan Ellison\, presi
 dent of the Elk Knob Community Heritage Organization (EKCHO) at EKCHO@gmai
 l.com. \nThe event is free and open to the public.
GEO:36.333462;-81.696432
LOCATION:Elk Knob State Park
