 ing\, and you need to know how to decipher a message written in invisible 
 ink. Supplies include a paint brush\, water\, drying cloth\, vitriol (dilu
 ted sulfuric acid)\, Thomas Jefferson cipher and “furnace box.” Read t
 he clues to find the coin with a hidden message\, reveal the message using
  the brush and vitriol\, then use the cipher to decode the message.\n\nCon
 tact: Nancy Locquet Absillis\, nancy.locquet@naturalsciences.org
