DESCRIPTION:Event is free but pre-registration is required since space is l
 imited to 26 participants. Register to reserve your space on a Big Canoe a
 t this link.\n\nLocation:  Robeson Creek Boat Ramp\, Hanks Chapel Road\, P
 ittsboro (GPS 35.70393\, -79.10015). Please note this is the Boat Ramp\, n
 ot the Canoe Access that is also on Hanks Chapel Road. \n\nFriends of Lowe
 r Haw is partnering with NC State Parks to offer a free Big Canoes paddle 
 during the full moon. NC State Parks will be bringing 2 of their 29-foot B
 ig Canoes. This Big Canoes trip is suitable for children and adults – a 
 great outing for families! Life jackets for children and adults will be pr
 ovided. All ages are welcome\, but young children who are unable to paddle
  or keep themselves upright will need to be accompanied by a parent or gua
 rdian. Guides will be Sean Higgins with NC State Parks Interpretation & Ed
 ucation and volunteers with Friends of Lower Haw. We will take a leisurely
  paddle on Robeson Creek to where it joins the Haw River. Round trip lasts
  about 1.5 hours.
GEO:35.717374;-79.139302
LOCATION:Robeson Creek Boat Ramp on Hanks Chapel Road
SUMMARY:Big Canoes Full Moon Paddle
