DESCRIPTION:This short guided night hike will lead you from the historic Ho
 rton Grove slave quarters through a nearby trail. During our walk\, we wil
 l focus on seeing\, listening\, and sensing the forest at night. Along the
  way\, your guide will pause for moments of reflection to read excerpts fr
 om North Carolina slave narratives. Discover how enslaved North Carolinian
 s used night as a time for refuge and resistance. As we finish the trail w
 alk\, you will view the rising full moon at Horton Grove. \n\nWe invite yo
 u to linger for quiet reflection\, or history Q and A with our guides\, af
 ter the hike ends. \n\nCome prepared for night walking and weather! We'll 
 meet at sunset and hike as the night darkens. We will walk about 1.3 miles
  at a slow pace\, with stops along the way. \n\nRegistration:\n\nYou must 
 register in advance to join this hike! Space is limited. To register\, ple
 ase email your name\, email contact\, and requested number of attendees to
  stagville@dncr.nc.gov. Space is limited for this small group experience\,
  and your registration is not confirmed until you receive a confirmation e
 mail from our staff. \n\nKnow Before You Go:\n\nBring your own headlamp or
  flashlight(s). We will intentionally pause and turn off all lights to be 
 in darkness at several points during the program.Dress for the weather and
  wear walking shoes!No restrooms are available on the site\, so prepare ah
 ead.This event includes walking about 1.3 miles\, with uneven dirt and gra
 ss surfaces. The trail has no major elevation changes.This program is reco
 mmended for ages 12 and up. Questions? Contact Historic Stagville staff at
  stagville@dncr.nc.gov or 919-620-0120.
GEO:36.115365;-78.841527
LOCATION:Historic Stagville\, Horton Grove - 5925 Jock Road
SUMMARY:Full Moon & Freedom Stories Night Hike - Stagville
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/full-moon-freedom-stories-ni
 ght-hike-stagville
