DESCRIPTION:Join the Charlotte Hawkins Brown Museum (CHB)\, Planted Soul Li
 fe\, and the North Carolina Cooperative Extension for “Palmer Presents: 
 Let’s Grow Together\,” a fall gardening workshop. This free event will
  take place at the CHB picnic shelter on Saturday\, Aug. 29\, from 10 a.m.
 -1 p.m. This immersive experience will also highlight the history and impo
 rtance of agriculture at Palmer Memorial Institute. CHB is administered by
  the Division of State Historic Sites within the N.C. Department of Natura
 l and Cultural Resources (DNCR).\n\nAttendees will learn about best practi
 ces for fall planting\, the benefits of houseplants\, and home gardening t
 echniques. Participants can start a 5-gallon grow bag to take home and are
  encouraged to get their hands dirty in the CHB community garden. The work
 shop will close with a seed swap and an invitation to taste items grown in
  partner gardens. Kids are welcome!\n\nFamilies\, individuals\, and groups
  should register in advance online: https://tinyurl.com/CHBFallGarden2026.
  The first 30 participants to sign up will receive growing materials to ta
 ke home.
GEO:36.067925;-79.624279
LOCATION:Charlotte Hawkins Brown Museum
SUMMARY:CHB Museum: Let's Grow Together: A Fall Garden Workshop
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/chb-lets-grow-together-a-fal
 l-garden-workshop
