UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53506303625806
DTSTART:20260905T140000Z
DTEND:20260905T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Fort Fisher State Historic Site on September 5\, 202
 6 for a special pop-up event about our favorite furry friends!\n\nDiscover
  the stories of the pets\, mascots\, and other animals that left their mar
 k on the Civil War. Learn how these faithful companions provided comfort\,
  companionship\, and a sense of humanity to soldiers\, and hear about the 
 animals that belonged to individual soldiers\, entire companies\, and thos
 e that called Fort Fisher home.\n\nStop by to dive deeper\, and explore ho
 w community partners in and around Wilmington provide care for animals tod
 ay! Learn from special displays about how humans and animals interact at h
 ome and in the wild. You might even meet a furry friend looking for a fore
 ver home!\n\nLeashed pets are welcome and encouraged outdoors and on the w
 alking trails. Please note that only service animals are permitted to ente
 r the Visitor Center.\n\nPlease consider carpooling with friends and famil
 y wherever possible! Limited extra parking is available at Battle Acre Roa
 d. The gate to the main parking lot is to be locked at 5:00pm.\n\nAll even
 ts are subject to change or cancellation. Stay tuned to our social media f
 or more information as we approach September 5!
GEO:33.971637;-77.91773
LOCATION:Fort Fisher Historic Site
SUMMARY:Furry Friends at Fort Fisher
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/furry-friends-at-fort-fisher
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Special Site Programs
END:VEVENT
