DESCRIPTION:Join us as we celebrate the Auger Hole Trail at Gorges State Pa
 rk in Transylvania County!\n\nPlease meet at the Frozen Creek Trailhead at
  1:00 pm on September 11 for a 2 hr event including a dedication of the fo
 rest into the Old-Growth Forest Network and guided experience on the Auger
  Hole Trail\, one of the few old-growth forests left in Transylvania Count
 y. This program is free and open to the public\, but spots are limited to 
 20 people for the guided hike. The total hike is approximately 2 miles wit
 h moderate difficulty and elevation gain.\n\nPlease Register using the att
 ached Eventbrite link. \n\nPlease note: parking is limited so this event i
 s limited to 20 attendees. Please carpool if possible and register all gue
 sts intending to attend.\n\nPhoto courtesy of Elizabeth Whitley.
GEO:35.119856;-82.869194
LOCATION:Gorges State Park - Frozen Creek Access\, Frozen Creek Access\, Au
 ger Hole Trailhead
SUMMARY:Old Growth Forest Network Dedication Event - Gorges State Park
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/old-growth-forest-network-de
 dication-event-gorges-state-park
