DESCRIPTION:North Carolina is home to many native ferns and Occoneechee Mou
 ntain is certainly no exception. Join a Ranger for a short hike to see how
  many we can find.\n\nAll children must be accompanied by an adult. Please
  be sure to dress appropriately for the weather\, wear hiking shoes\, wear
  bug spray\, and bring water! Be prepared to hike off trail. We will also 
 be using the seek app by iNaturalist to identify a lot of ferns\; you may 
 want to download the app if you don't already have it.\n\nSpaces are limit
 ed\, and registration is required. To sign up\, call (984) 250-1370 or ema
 il eno.river@ncparks.gov. Include the number of guests in your party and a
  phone number where you can be reached if the event is changed or canceled
 .
GEO:36.059593;-79.113906
LOCATION:Occoneechee Mountain State Natural Area\, Eno Mountain Rd. Access
SUMMARY:Forest Feathers
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/forest-feathers
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
