UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53118256855682
DTSTART:20260913T180000Z
DTEND:20260913T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:Here's an opportunity to learn about a part of our history you 
 may not have known. Join the New Bern Historical on Sunday\, Sept. 13 at 2
 pm at Orringer Auditorium at Craven Community College when they will host 
 Dr. Valerie Johnson as she presents "The Harlowe Patriots". It's a little 
 known but important piece of American history: black soldiers fighting aga
 inst the British in the Revolutionary War. It's estimated that 5\,000 blac
 k soldiers served on the Patriot side during the Revolution\, which lasted
  from 1775 to 1783.Fourteen free men of color from the Harlowe community o
 f Havelock fought in key battles of the war\, with General George Washingt
 on leading the fight for independence. Join Dr. Johnson as she reveals thi
 s important story and its connection to us today.
GEO:35.111074;-77.103209
LOCATION:Orringer Auditorium
SUMMARY:The Harlowe Patriots
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/the-harlowe-patriots
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041836Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53046287107616
DTSTART:20260913T180000Z
DTEND:20260913T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:HARLOWE\, Craven County - It's a little known but important pie
 ce of American history: black soldiers fighting against the British in the
  Revolutionary War. It's estimated that 5\,000 black soldiers served on th
 e Patriot side during the Revolution\, which lasted from 1775 to 1783.Four
 teen free men of color from the Harlowe community of Havelock fought in ke
 y battles of the war\, with General George Washington leading the fight fo
 r independence. Join the New Bern Historical Society as they host Dr. Vale
 rie Johnson as she shares this important story from local history on Sunda
 y\, September 13\, 2026 at 2pm at Orringer Auditorium at Craven Community 
 College.  Learn about these 14 brave men and the folks that discovered the
 ir story and the families that are still here.
GEO:35.111074;-77.103209
LOCATION:Orringer Auditorium\, Craven Community College
SUMMARY:The Harlowe Patriots by Dr. Valerie Johnson
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/the-harlowe-patriots-by-dr-v
 alerie-johnson
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041836Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53763076260134
DTSTART:20260913T200000Z
DTEND:20260913T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:On the afternoon of Sunday September 13th\, bring the whole fam
 ily and make memories as we celebrate Grandparents Day! Spend the evening 
 enjoying Lake James State Park and making memories. \n\nWhether you're an 
 experienced angler or fishing for the first time\, this is a wonderful opp
 ortunity for grandparents\, grandchildren\, parents\, and friends to enjoy
  a relaxing day together at beautiful Lake James State Park. Don't let not
  having the proper tackle stop you from joining us because we can provide 
 rods and basic tackle to use through our tackle loaner program.\n\nThings 
 to bring/know: Children must be accompanied by an adult at all times\, NCW
 RC fishing regulations will apply\, bring tackle and bait if you have it b
 ut we will have some available to use\, water\, sunscreen\, and ready to h
 ave a great time.\n\nAgenda: Meet the Ranger at Lake James State Park Visi
 tor Center at the Paddy's Creek Access at 4:00PM to learn about the lake a
 nd the fish that call Lake James home. After a short talk and making sure 
 everybody has the necessary tackle\, the Ranger will lead all participants
  to the fishing pier where the Ranger will provide hints\, tips\, and help
  to the participants. There is no timeframe so you are free to leave when 
 you like or explore other areas of the park to test out your newfound fish
 ing knowledge.
GEO:35.760718;-81.882276
LOCATION:Lake James State Park - Paddy's Creek Access\, Visitor Center
SUMMARY:Grandparents and Fishing 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/grandparents-and-fishing
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Outdoor Recreation (kayak\, paddle\, hikes)
CATEGORIES:Nature & Wildlife Programs
CATEGORIES:Youth & Family Activities
END:VEVENT
