DESCRIPTION:Join the Charlotte Hawkins Brown Museum and Dr. Worth Hayes vir
 tually as we explore the life and work of Doris Allen Anderson\, founder a
 nd leader of the Howalton Day School in Chicago\, IL. This school and its 
 progressive curriculum was a haven for Chicago's Black community from 1946
  to 1999. Dr. Worth K. Hayes\, author of Schools of Our Own: Chicago’s G
 olden Age of Black Private Education and a coming biography of Doris Allen
  Anderson\, will lead this conversation. We are excited to host you in our
  salon!
