DESCRIPTION:Celebrate National Public Lands Day with a Tails & Trails Quest
 !\n\nLooking for a fun way to celebrate National Public Lands Day? Join us
  for the next Tails & Trails Quest on Saturday\, September 26 at 10:00 am 
 presented by Friends of the Fonta Flora State Trail and Lake James State P
 ark.\n\nThis self-guided adventure takes place along the Holly Discovery T
 rail\, a scenic\, family-friendly\, one-mile loop that's perfect for hiker
 s of all ages (and their four-legged friends!).\n\nAlong the trail you'll 
 discover:\n- Interactive educational stations\n- A fun quest to complete F
 ascinating facts about the plants\, wildlife\, and natural history of Lake
  James\n- Learn more about the growing Fonta Flora State Trail and how it'
 s connecting communities across Western North Carolina.\n\nWhether you're 
 exploring with your kids\, walking the dog\, or simply looking for a beaut
 iful way to spend the day outdoors\, this event is designed to help you co
 nnect with nature while supporting the future of trails in our region.\n\n
 Event Details\n- Saturday\, September 26\n- Holly Discovery Trail\, Lake J
 ames State Park\n- Approximately 1-mile loop\n- Family-friendly\n- Dog-fri
 endly\n- Free to participate\n\nCome celebrate our public lands\, enjoy on
 e of North Carolina's most beautiful state parks\, and discover why every 
 mile of the Fonta Flora State Trail matters.\n\nWe hope to see you on the 
 trail!
GEO:35.760718;-81.882276
LOCATION:Lake James State Park - Paddy's Creek Access
SUMMARY:Tails & Trails Quest
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/tails-trails-quest
