DTSTAMP:20260905T041837Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53312428110280
DTSTART:20261003T140000Z
DTEND:20261003T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the Catawba Cultural Center\, Kings Mountai
 n Historical Museum is excited to present\, "Choosing Sides: The Catawba N
 ation & the Fight for Independence." This exhibit explores the critical ro
 le of the Catawba Nation\, also known as Yį Iswąre or “People of the R
 iver\,” in the American Revolutionary War\, particularly in the backcoun
 try regions of Tryon and Lincoln Counties. As skilled warriors\, guides\, 
 and allies of the Patriot cause\, the Catawba people defended their homela
 nd\, protected settler communities\, and contributed to pivotal battles. D
 espite the hardships of disease\, displacement\, and warfare\, the Catawba
  demonstrated extraordinary resilience. Their story is one of courage\, al
 liance\, and survival\, woven into the struggle for independence in the So
 uthern Campaign of the Revolution.\n\nThe exhibit will run from June 30\, 
 2026 until October 24\, 2026. Admission is Free!
GEO:35.239004;-81.342181
LOCATION:Kings Mountain Historical Museum
SUMMARY:Choosing Sides: The Catawba Nation & The Fight for Independence
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/choosing-sides-the-catawba-n
 ation-the-fight-for-independence
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041837Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53138241972242
DTSTART:20261003T140000Z
DTEND:20261003T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
  at the Gregg Museum of Art & Design presents a series of vignettes explor
 ing spaces of dignity\, belonging\, safety\, and imagination within Black 
 communities across North Carolina. Featuring historical photographs\, cont
 emporary images\, artworks from the Gregg Museum collection including a ha
 ndmade guitar by Freeman Vines\, and ephemera from community partners\, th
 e exhibition reflects on place\, memory\, creativity\, and spiritual resil
 ience across generations. Through stories of triumph and adversity\, Commu
 nity Stories honors the ways Black Americans have sustained and uplifted t
 heir communities through family\, entrepreneurship\, cultural expression\,
  and soulful imagination\, while inspiring future generations.
GEO:35.784925;-78.661662
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining
 -north-carolinas-black-heritage
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
