UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53514203945302
DTSTART:20261003T140000Z
DTEND:20261003T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:A day of vintage base ball played at the Historic Durham Athlet
 ic Park !\n\n***Any tickets purchased for our 2025 Vintage Base Ball event
  are valid for 2026!***\n\nThe iconic Durham Athletic Park has hosted base
 ball games since 1926 and was even featured in an iconic baseball film\, b
 ut Durham’s baseball roots are even deeper. The first century of basebal
 l was marked by racial segregation and separate leagues for black and whit
 e athletes at the DAP until the 1950s\; however\, Duke Homestead welcomes 
 all people to participate and honors the struggles and achievements of the
  many players over the past century who brought us the Durham baseball cul
 ture we know today. Players will wear historic uniforms\, follow historic 
 gameplay\, and use historic equipment. The games will follow 1860 and 1869
  Beadles Rules.\n\nWe invite you to connect with the history of this sport
 \, this place\, and this community by enjoying an afternoon out at the bal
 l park.\n\nAdmission to the game is $10\; children under 4 years old will 
 be admitted free. Game tickets can be purchased online through Eventbrite\
 , or in person at the Duke Homestead visitor center\, as well as at the ga
 te on game day. Early-Bird tickets for $5 available until 9/21 (online her
 e or at the Duke Homestead visitor center).\n\nEnjoy a family-friendly day
  at the ball park complete with “old fashioned” concessions\, food\, b
 eer\, and historic music. Spectators are encouraged to come dressed in you
 r favorite historical\, vintage\, or retro inspired outfits. We believe in
  vintage style\, not vintage values! Kids will get to play historic games 
 with our costumed interpreters\, as well as have the opportunity to run th
 e bases in-between ball games.\n\nJoining our local Duke Homestead team th
 is year will be The Shiners from Rockingham\, VA and a special team from t
 he Durham Fire Department! The first game will be played at 11am\, with ga
 mes at 12:30pm and 2pm to follow.\n\nThis game is a fundraiser for the Duk
 e Homestead State Historic Site and it is sponsored by the Duke Homestead 
 Education and History Corporation (the site’s volunteer\, non-profit sup
 port organization)\, Measurement\, Inc.\, and Stone Brothers & Byrd.\n\nFr
 ee parking available at the lot at 412 Morris St\, Durham\, NC 27701. A co
 uple of handicap spaces are available in the DAP parking lot.\n\n**We are 
 unable to offer refunds on purchased tickets. All cancelled tickets will b
 e considered a donation to the site and will be used for future educationa
 l programming.**
GEO:36.002299;-78.903162
LOCATION:Historic Durham Athletic Park
SUMMARY:Vintage Base Ball Day at the DAP
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/vintage-base-ball-day-at-the
 -dap
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
END:VEVENT
