BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041837Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53613870680968
DTSTART:20261010T140000Z
DTEND:20261010T153000Z
DESCRIPTION:Cape Fear Legends & Lore – October 10 – 10 am and 12 noon\n
 \nGet to know the Cape Fear’s most enduring legends with this special cr
 uise charting the stories that don’t always get told. From the tunnels u
 nderneath the city to the colonial imposter who tempted fate by claiming t
 o be royal\, this cruise will traverse the last 250 years of local history
  to get at the heart of what’s fact and what’s fiction. Were rum runne
 rs captured on the river during Prohibition? Did Lord Cornwallis during hi
 s Revolutionary War visit to town occupy a downtown house and let his sold
 iers crash on the property while keeping Patriot prisoners in the basement
 ? And the time Yellow Fever turned the city into a ghost town\, and the re
 bellious age of Prohibition. We will answer those and more!  Hunter Ingram
 \, historian at Burgwin-Wright House\, will share these stories and more. 
 This is a 90 minute cruise $40. Boarding is 15 minutes prior to departure.
  There is a second cruise on this date at Noon as well.
LOCATION:Wilmington Water Tours\, On the Riverwalk
SUMMARY:Cape Fear Legends & Lore River Cruise
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/cape-fear-legends-lore-river
 -cruise
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041837Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53312428115405
DTSTART:20261010T140000Z
DTEND:20261010T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the Catawba Cultural Center\, Kings Mountai
 n Historical Museum is excited to present\, "Choosing Sides: The Catawba N
 ation & the Fight for Independence." This exhibit explores the critical ro
 le of the Catawba Nation\, also known as Yį Iswąre or “People of the R
 iver\,” in the American Revolutionary War\, particularly in the backcoun
 try regions of Tryon and Lincoln Counties. As skilled warriors\, guides\, 
 and allies of the Patriot cause\, the Catawba people defended their homela
 nd\, protected settler communities\, and contributed to pivotal battles. D
 espite the hardships of disease\, displacement\, and warfare\, the Catawba
  demonstrated extraordinary resilience. Their story is one of courage\, al
 liance\, and survival\, woven into the struggle for independence in the So
 uthern Campaign of the Revolution.\n\nThe exhibit will run from June 30\, 
 2026 until October 24\, 2026. Admission is Free!
GEO:35.239004;-81.342181
LOCATION:Kings Mountain Historical Museum
SUMMARY:Choosing Sides: The Catawba Nation & The Fight for Independence
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/choosing-sides-the-catawba-n
 ation-the-fight-for-independence
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
