DESCRIPTION:Join the NC Museum of Natural Sciences as they search for the m
 ajestic elk\, reintroduced to the Great Smoky Mountains National Park afte
 r an absence of more than 200 years. Observe and learn about elk biology\,
  while also exploring other facets of the Park’s ecosystem. Sample some 
 activities used to document the biodiversity of the Park. Participate in c
 itizen science data collection on snails and lichens. Discover how you can
  bring the excitement of field research into your classroom.\n\nCredit: 20
  contact hours toward CEUs or Criteria II/III for North Carolina’s Envir
 onmental Education Certification Program\n\nLodging: The workshop fee cove
 rs a two-night stay in a lodge in Lake Junaluska\, NC. Most rooms will be 
 double occupancy.\n\nTransportation: Participants can ride with the group 
 from Raleigh departing at 2pm or meet us at the lodging in Lake Junaluska 
 in the evening. Transportation will be in Museum vans.\n\nRegistration: Re
 gister here online\n\nThe full workshop fee is due when you register and p
 ayment is via credit card. Registration for most Educator Treks is on a fi
 rst-come\, first-served basis. Treks fill quickly\, so register early! IF 
 you find the program is full when you attempt to register\, please sign up
  for the waiting list! We frequently have turnover and often pull from the
  waiting list. We will let you know as soon as possible if a spot opens fo
 r you.\n\nAdditional Details:\n\nFee: $160 (includes lodging\, some meals\
 , transportation\, and classroom resources)Requirements: For educators (in
 cludes teachers\, administrators\, pre-service or substitute teachers\; no
 n-formal educators\; anyone working on their EE certification)Program Inst
 ructor(s): Megan Davis\, Rory McCollumActivity Level: Moderate (hiking up 
 to two miles on uneven trails)\n Note: We do not want cost to be a barrier
  for any educator. If the cost of this workshop would prevent your partici
 pation\, please reach out to Megan Davis. The cost of this workshop is sub
 sidized by the Teacher Education fund at the NCMNS.
LOCATION:Great Smoky Mountains National Park
SUMMARY:Educator Trek: Got Elk?
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/educator-trek-got-elk
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
