UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51498196145905
DTSTART:20261107T230000Z
DTEND:20261108T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:This event is free to attend\, but registration is requested. \
 n\nJoin local astronomers with the Greensboro Astronomy Club as we observe
  the night skies over the Iron Ore Belt Access. Attendees may expect to se
 e closer-than-typical views of the moon\, planets\, star clusters\, and ot
 her celestial objects subject to change with time of year and local sky da
 rkness.\n\nTelescopes and viewing equipment will be set up on site but you
  may wish to bring your own binoculars or telescope\, plus a chair or blan
 ket for seating. Dress for the weather. Flashlights & headlamps should hav
 e a red-light option or filter to protect your night vision.\n\nSkywatchin
 g sessions may be cancelled at the last minute for weather. Please registe
 r at the Register link so you can be emailed in the event of cancellation.
 \n\nProgram equipment and instruction provided by members of the Greensbor
 o Astronomy Club\, which meet the third Friday of each month at the Greens
 boro Science Center. Learn more about their organization here: \n\nhttps:/
 /greensboroastronomyclub.org/\n\nStar-gazing Etiquette:\n\nPlease use a re
 d light at the observing session and keep any light pointed at the ground.
  As your eyes adapt\, a light is not needed at all.Pease do not touch any 
 telescopes or other equipment unless permission is given and form a orderl
 y line behind each telescope. Please do not allow children or pets to run 
 around the observing area. Pets must be on a leash no longer than 6 feet a
 t all times. This is to protect others' safety and the equipment.Stock pho
 to © Pexels / Lucas Pezeta
GEO:36.23742;-79.785591
LOCATION:Haw River State Park - Iron Ore Belt Access 
SUMMARY:Deep Sky Astronomy
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/copy-of-deep-sky-astronomy-3
 512
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
