UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51851019111989
DTSTART:20261213T180000Z
DTEND:20261213T223000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us once again this holiday season\, as we explore how the 
 American colonists celebrated Christmas. During the program\, you can enjo
 y 18th-century-inspired refreshments in the Visitor Center\, participate i
 n traditional games\, or try your hand at Moravian paper stars and other 1
 8th-century crafts. The highlight of the evening will be an authentic\nper
 iod candlelit service in the ruins of St. Philip's Anglican Church. The se
 rvice will begin at 5:00pm and will conclude by 5:30pm. Tickets can be pur
 chased at the gate on the day of.\n$5 per person.
GEO:34.040206;-77.946023
LOCATION:Brunswick Town/Fort Anderson
SUMMARY:An 18th Century Christmas
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/an-18th-century-christmas
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
END:VEVENT
