BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041839Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52312397324244
DTSTART:20270620T140000Z
DTEND:20270620T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Battle of Ramsour’s Mill Living History Weekend commemora
 tes the June 20\, 1780 Battle of Ramsour’s Mill\, when Whigs met Tories 
 on a hillside just outside the little town of Lincolnton.\n\nIn 2026\, the
  commemoration will take place the weekend of June 20 & 21 near Battlegrou
 nd Elementary School.\n\nIn between\, hearth cooking demonstrations by the
  Lincoln County Hearth Cooks\, reenactments and weapons demonstrations\, a
  militia encampment\, speakers and storytellers\, heritage demonstrations\
 , battleground tours\, and period crafts. All activities are free.\n\nSche
 dule is subject to change. Reenactors and demonstrators welcome! Reenactor
 s who wish to participate should contact Lisa Pupkiewicz at lpupkie@gmail.
 com\; suttlers should contact Beverly Moore at bkingnccp@gmail.com
GEO:35.479393;-81.260402
LOCATION:Ramsour's Mill
SUMMARY:Battle of Ramsour's Mill 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/battle-of-ramsours-mill
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Festivals & Fairs
CATEGORIES:Ceremonies & Anniversaries
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041839Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51950900573619
DTSTART:20270624T140000Z
DTEND:20270624T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Explore the diverse stories of those who called North Carolina 
 home during the American Revolution in this compelling traveling exhibit. 
 People of Colonial North Carolina highlights the complex and often conflic
 ting paths different communities took in the fight for freedom and surviva
 l. Through maps\, rare documents\, and illustrations\, the exhibit offers 
 a look at how the American Revolution impacted everyday lives.
GEO:36.092774;-79.436435
LOCATION:May Memorial Library
SUMMARY:People of Colonial North Carolina Exhibit
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/people-of-colonial-north-car
 olina
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
